## Complete Investigation Report

I've thoroughly investigated the icon system in the pantoken repo. Here's what I found:

### **1. Where Icons Are Sourced & Registered**

**Canonical InstUI Icons (Custom + Lucide)** — [packages/core/src/icons.ts](packages/core/src/icons.ts)
- **Line 96-120**: `readCustomGlyphs()` reads SVG files from `@instructure/ui-icons/svg/Custom`
- **Line 122-185**: `readLucideGlyphs()` reads Lucide icons wrapped by InstUI
- **Line 236-240**: `collectIcons()` function merges them using a Map:
  ```ts
  if (uiIconsRoot && includeLucide) {
    for (const t of readLucideGlyphs(uiIconsRoot, bidi)) byName.set(t.name, t);  // Line 236
  }
  if (uiIconsRoot && includeInstui) {
    // Custom overrides Lucide on name collisions.
    for (const t of readCustomGlyphs(uiIconsRoot, bidi)) byName.set(t.name, t);  // Line 239
  }
  ```
  **Result: Custom glyphs win over Lucide** ✓

**Simple-icons Plugin** — [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts)
- **Lines 136-156**: Token hook appends simple-icons to token array:
  ```ts
  return [...tokens, ...additions.map((a) => defineToken(a))];  // Line 156
  ```

**Lucide-lab Plugin** — [plugins/pantoken/lucide-lab/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/lucide-lab/src/index.ts)
- **Lines 107-122**: Token hook appends lucide-lab icons:
  ```ts
  return [...tokens, ...additions.map((token) => defineToken(token))];  // Line 122
  ```

**Simple-icons Manifest** — [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/scripts/generate-manifest.ts](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/scripts/generate-manifest.ts)
- **Lines 18-28**: Generates flat array of all simple-icons slugs (no deduplication)

---

### **2. How Icon Names Are Normalized**

- **InstUI icons**: Use kebab-case, read from file names, stored as `--instui-icon-{name}`
  - Examples: `arrow-left`, `circle-question-mark` ([packages/core/src/icons.ts](packages/core/src/icons.ts#L97))
- **Simple-icons**: Slug-based from simple-icons npm package (kebab-case by design)
  - Converted to export name then back to kebab-case via `toExportName()` ([plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts#L42-L50))
- **Lucide-lab**: CamelCase export names converted to kebab-case via `toKebab()` ([plugins/pantoken/lucide-lab/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/lucide-lab/src/index.ts#L42-L49))

---

### **3. Where & How Icon Sets Get Merged**

**At Build Time (Core Plugin Pipeline)**
- **File**: [packages/core/src/plugin.ts](packages/core/src/plugin.ts)
- **Function** `runIconPlugins()` **lines 186-221**:
  ```ts
  let added: Token[] = [];
  for (const plugin of active) {
    const result = plugin.icons?.({ icons: existingIcons, theme });
    if (!Array.isArray(result)) continue;
    for (const entry of result) {
      const token = iconEntryToToken(sanitized);
      if (token) added.push(token);
    }
  }
  return added.length ? dedupeByName([...tokens, ...added]) : tokens;  // Line 220
  ```
  Each plugin's icons hook is called in order, results appended to `added[]`, then `dedupeByName()` is called **keeping the last occurrence**.

- **Function** `runTokenPlugins()` **lines 121-150**:
  ```ts
  let acc = tokens;
  for (const plugin of checkPlugins(plugins, "tokens")) {
    const result = plugin.tokens?.({ tokens: acc, theme });
    // ... validation ...
    acc = validated;  // Replace with plugin's result
  }
  return dedupeByName(acc);  // Line 149 — keep last occurrence
  ```

**At Runtime (TinyMCE Renderer)**
- **File**: [renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts)
- **Function** `loadAllIcons()` **lines 63-99**:
  ```ts
  const icons: TaggedIcon[] = [];

  // 1. Load components from @pantoken/tokens
  for (const token of rebrandTokens) {
    if (token.meta?.kind !== "icon" || !token.name.startsWith(COMPONENT_ICON_TOKEN_PREFIX))
      continue;
    icons.push({ name, source: "components", ... });  // Line 67-69
  }

  // 2. Load simple-icons
  for (const iconSlug of simpleIconsManifest) {
    icons.push({ name: iconSlug, source: "simple-icons", ... });  // Line 72-76
  }

  // 3. Load lucide-lab
  for (const iconName of lucideLabManifest) {
    icons.push({ name: iconName, source: "lucide-lab", ... });  // Line 79-83
  }

  // 4. Load custom-icons
  for (const icon of customIconsList) {
    icons.push({ name: icon.name, source: "custom-icons", ... });  // Line 86-88
  }

  return icons.sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));  // Line 99 — NO DEDUPLICATION
  ```
  **Result: ALL sources are appended to a single array, sorted by name. Duplicates can exist with different `source` values.**

---

### **4. Build-Time vs Runtime Merging**

**Build-Time** — [formats/tokens/scripts/generate.ts](formats/tokens/scripts/generate.ts)
- **Lines 145-160**: Canonical IR built with:
  ```ts
  const base = buildTokens({
    theme,
    resolveModifierIssue: (issue) => { ... },
    // Note: NO plugins parameter
  });
  ```
  **The canonical `@pantoken/tokens` IR contains ONLY InstUI icons (Custom + Lucide merged), no simple-icons or lucide-lab plugins.**

**Runtime** — [renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts)
- Icons from different sources are loaded and merged at render time by `loadAllIcons()`.
- Simple-icons + lucide-lab are NOT in the canonical IR; they're loaded separately.

---

### **5. Existing Conflict-Resolution Logic**

**In Core Plugin System** — [packages/core/src/plugin.ts](packages/core/src/plugin.ts#L60-L74)
- Comment line 60: `"De-duplicate tokens by name, keeping the last occurrence (so later plugins win)."`
- `dedupeByName()` function lines 60-67: Creates a Map by token name, keeps only the last value
  ```ts
  export function dedupeByName(tokens: Token[]): Token[] {
    const byName = new Map<string, Token>();
    for (const token of tokens) byName.set(token.name, token);
    return [...byName.values()];
  }
  ```
  **Principle: Later sources/plugins win over earlier ones.**

**In TinyMCE** — [renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts#L125-L169)
- `getUsedIconCdnFiles()` function handles **used** icons (those with `-icon-*` classes in the DOM):
  ```ts
  const icon = candidates.find((candidate) =>
    currentAssetKeys.has(assetKey(getIconCdnFile(candidate))),
  );
  return [getIconCdnFile(icon ?? candidates[0])];  // Line 162-164
  ```
  **Tie-breaker: If icon name exists in multiple sources, use the one already loaded, or pick first candidate.**

---

### **6. Tests for Icon Name Conflicts**

**TinyMCE Icon Tests** — [renderers/tinymce/tests/icons.test.ts](renderers/tinymce/tests/icons.test.ts)
- Line 14: `"loadAllIcons returns icons from all four providers, sorted by name"` — just checks loading works, no collision test
- Line 110: `"getUsedIconCdnFiles preserves the selected provider for duplicate icon names"` — tests that when an icon name is in multiple sources and already loaded, the loaded one is kept

**Example from test** (lines 110-121):
```ts
test("getUsedIconCdnFiles preserves the selected provider for duplicate icon names", () => {
  const icons: TaggedIcon[] = [
    { name: "heart", source: "components" },
    { name: "heart", source: "simple-icons" },  // SAME NAME, different source
  ];
  const template = document.createElement("template");
  template.innerHTML = '<span class="-icon-heart"></span>';

  expect(
    getUsedIconCdnFiles(template.content, icons, [
      { package: "@pantoken/plugin-simple-icons", path: "dist/icons/heart.css" },
    ]),
  ).toEqual([{ package: "@pantoken/plugin-simple-icons", path: "dist/icons/heart.css" }]);
  // When simple-icons is already loaded, simple-icons:heart is used (not components:heart)
});
```

**No `x` icon collision test found**, but the infrastructure exists to handle duplicates.

---

### **7. Current Merge Order & Bug Confirmation**

**In TinyMCE Picker (`loadAllIcons`)**:
1. Components (InstUI) — line 67-69
2. Simple-icons — line 72-76
3. Lucide-lab — line 79-83
4. Custom-icons — line 86-88
5. **Then sorted alphabetically by name** — line 99

**For an icon named `x`:**
- If `x` exists in both components (InstUI) and simple-icons, `loadAllIcons()` returns **both**:
  ```
  [
    { name: "x", source: "components", ... },
    { name: "x", source: "simple-icons", ... },
    ...
  ]
  ```
- When sorted by name, they end up adjacent
- When `buildEmoticonsDatabase()` creates picker entries (line 172-182), both are added with keys like `components:x` and `simple-icons:x`
- In the picker UI, **both sources would be visible for the same icon name**
- When inserted via `getUsedIconCdnFiles()` (line 162), **the first candidate (`components:x`) would be picked** if it's not already loaded

**Confirmed issue**: Simple-icons is loaded AFTER components in `loadAllIcons()`, so if you start fresh without any assets already loaded:
- `candidates[0]` is `components:x` ✓ (this would actually work correctly)
- But if simple-icons CSS was already loaded, it would stick: `candidates.find()` would return the one in `currentAssets`

**The real problem**: The picker UI shows BOTH sources for duplicate names, and the selection logic is confusing. User wants a clear precedence: **InstUI icons always win, simple-icons are secondary/only used if no InstUI equivalent exists.**

---

## Summary Table

| Aspect | Details | File | Lines |
|--------|---------|------|-------|
| **InstUI icon merge** | Custom overrides Lucide | [packages/core/src/icons.ts](packages/core/src/icons.ts) | 236-240 |
| **Simple-icons plugin** | Appends to token array | [plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/simple-icons/src/index.ts) | 156 |
| **Lucide-lab plugin** | Appends to token array | [plugins/pantoken/lucide-lab/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/lucide-lab/src/index.ts) | 122 |
| **Plugin deduplication** | Keep last occurrence | [packages/core/src/plugin.ts](packages/core/src/plugin.ts) | 60-74 |
| **TinyMCE merge** | Append all, NO dedup | [renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/icons.ts) | 63-99 |
| **Canonical IR build** | No plugins applied | [formats/tokens/scripts/generate.ts](formats/tokens/scripts/generate.ts) | 145-160 |
| **Icon name normalization** | All use kebab-case | Various (see section 2) | — |
| **Collision test** | Tie-break with currentAssets | [renderers/tinymce/tests/icons.test.ts](renderers/tinymce/tests/icons.test.ts) | 110-121 |

---

**Fix recommendation ready**: The solution is to deduplicate `loadAllIcons()` result with a priority order (components > lucide-lab > custom-icons > simple-icons), allowing downstream code to be written once the precedence is clear.

